  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Recovery Rapid Readiness Support in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this project the impacts of COVID-19 in Ethiopia&apos;s implementation of climate change strategies and plans will be assessed to develop recovery options to accelerate the country&apos;s transition to a green economy and for the country to build back better. The identification and prioritisation of needed reforms and investments including possible sources of funding will also be undertaken.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is - The impact of COVID-19 on country&#x2019;s climate change strategies and plans as well as its opportunities elaborated to inform country program, strategic frameworks and address policy gaps and - At least one quality concept note developed supported by pre-feasibility study submitted to the GCF, supporting the priority measures under the National Green Resilient Recovery Strategy</narrative>
  </description>
